      "q": "Which federal agency spends the most on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense spends the most on contracts. The Department of Defense obligated $278B in FY2026 to date, which is the largest single agency obligation reported. Other large obligators include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $68B and the Department of Homeland Security at $57.6B."
